---
import Marketing from "../layouts/Marketing.astro";
import PageIntro from "../components/PageIntro.astro";

// DRAFT awaiting Vladimir's review (see docs/STATE.md). Plain-language terms written from docs/SPEC.md.
---
<Marketing
  title="Terms | Pairpoll"
  description="The rules for using Pairpoll: what you may upload, how long polls last, what happens to rule-breaking polls, and the limits of the free service."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <PageIntro title="Terms" lead="The rules for using Pairpoll, in plain words." />
    <div class="prose legal">
      <p class="legal-date">Last updated 19 November 2026</p>

      <h2>The service</h2>
      <p>
        Pairpoll lets you upload images or videos, share a link and let people rank them by picking one of two. It's free.
        It's provided as it is, without guarantees, and it may change or stop.
      </p>

      <h2>What you upload</h2>
      <p>Only upload files you have the right to share. Don't use Pairpoll for:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>anything illegal, or sexual content involving minors;</li>
        <li>harassing, threatening or exposing people;</li>
        <li>content that copies someone else's work without permission;</li>
        <li>malware, spam or attempts to break the service.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We may remove a poll or block an account that breaks these rules, without notice. Anyone can report a poll from the
        link on its page.
      </p>

      <h2>How long polls last</h2>
      <p>
        Every poll, with its files and votes, is deleted automatically 30 days after it was created. Keep your own copies
        of your files and any results you want to keep.
      </p>

      <h2>Limits</h2>
      <p>
        To keep the service free and fair, there are limits on file sizes, on how many polls you can make, and on voters per
        poll. The app shows them where they apply.
      </p>

      <h2>Voters</h2>
      <p>
        When you vote, the poll's creator sees the name you type and your top list. Don't type anything in your name you
        wouldn't want them to see.
      </p>

      <h2>API keys and agents</h2>
      <p>
        Treat API keys like passwords. You're responsible for what is done with your keys, including by AI agents you
        connect. You can revoke a key at any time in your account.
      </p>

      <h2>Liability</h2>
      <p>
        Pairpoll isn't liable for lost data, for decisions you make based on poll results, or for content other people
        upload, as far as the law allows.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        These terms may change. The date at the top shows the latest version. Questions: <a href="mailto:hello@pairpoll.com">hello@pairpoll.com</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Marketing>

<style>
  .legal {
    padding-bottom: var(--s-8);
  }

  .legal-date {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }
</style>
